            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Svartalfar first blades head guilds of svartalfar assassins, earning their position as the most skilled in the ways of the blade. Once in this position of leadership, a first blade is always one misstep away from being usurped.</p><hr /><p>In the First World's first few centuries, even before the full creation of the Universe, svartalfars lived among the other fey. No records exist of their exact appearance at that time, though many scholars believe they had typical elven features. At some point in the distant past, the majority of these svartalfars participated in some unknown heinous acts, and their entire people were summarily exiled to the Netherworld. That shadowy plane soon warped svartalfars in both body and mind, turning their skin pale gray and hairless and their thoughts cruel and practical. Present-day svartalfars are born with some innate shadow magic.</p>\n<p>Svartalfar communities in the Netherworld are small, featuring tall, slender buildings and subterranean chambers. The largest structures are operated by powerful guilds of assassins and bounty hunters that the community takes great pride in. Guild members are deadly serious about any contracts they agree upon, working with brutal efficiency to find (and often dispose of) their targets. When a svartalfar fails to complete their mission, they are usually publicly executed by their kin.</p>",
